# Literals that are DELIBERATELY public, even though leak-patterns.local matches
# them. Fixed strings (not regexes), one per line; blank lines and #-comments
# ignored. The export strips these from a matched line before deciding it is a
# leak, so the same pattern is still caught everywhere else.
#
# You need this as soon as you publish: your name belongs in LICENSE and your
# repo URL belongs in README, yet both match patterns you will have listed in
# leak-patterns.local. Without an entry here, export.sh refuses to build.
#
# Keep entries as SPECIFIC as possible. "Jane Doe" exempts one exact string;
# "Jane" would disable the name check everywhere, including in prose that names
# you by accident.
#
# Never exported.
#
# Examples -- replace with your own:
# Jane Doe
# github.com/janedoe/your-repo
